WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.614 --> 00:00:03.281
(bells ringing)

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.440
(chime music)

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.893
(people talking quietly)

00:04:20.700 --> 00:04:24.519
- [Man] Four, and then
four, and then (indistinct).

00:04:24.519 --> 00:04:27.186
(bells chiming)

00:09:29.079 --> 00:09:31.996
(people cheering)

00:09:39.052 --> 00:09:41.719
(bells chiming)

00:10:58.632 --> 00:11:00.882
(clapping)

00:11:23.372 --> 00:11:26.205
(people laughing)

00:11:27.172 --> 00:11:30.005
(people cheering)

00:11:52.305 --> 00:11:55.138
(people cheering)

00:13:15.388 --> 00:13:18.221
(people laughing)

00:13:46.012 --> 00:13:48.845
(people cheering)

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:21.713
(people clapping)

00:14:36.378 --> 00:14:39.211
(people laughing)

00:15:05.187 --> 00:15:08.020
(people cheering)

00:15:38.189 --> 00:15:41.022
(classical music)

00:19:11.337 --> 00:19:15.762
- Good afternoon, Yale
College class of 2021.

00:19:15.762 --> 00:19:18.595
(people cheering)

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:28.963
Welcome to the graduates
of Berkeley, Davenport,

00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:35.243
Benjamin Franklin, and
Pauli Murray Colleges,

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:41.319
and welcome to family, friends,
and members of the class

00:19:41.319 --> 00:19:45.580
who are joining us
virtually via livestream.

00:19:45.580 --> 00:19:48.763
We are so excited to have
arrived at this special day.

00:19:49.670 --> 00:19:52.500
In a few moments, we will
begin announcing the graduates

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.550
as they process across the
commencement stage here

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:58.990
in front of me, but before
we start our program,

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:01.360
a few words about the land on which

00:20:01.360 --> 00:20:04.460
today's ceremony is taking place.

00:20:04.460 --> 00:20:08.200
Yale acknowledges that
indigenous peoples and nations

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:12.633
including Mohegan, Mashantucket
Pequot, Eastern Pequot,

00:20:13.858 --> 00:20:17.290
Schaghticoke, Golden
Hill Paugussett, Niantic

00:20:18.450 --> 00:20:22.320
and the Quinnipiac and other
Algonquin-speaking peoples

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:25.880
have stewarded through generations,
the lands and waterways

00:20:25.880 --> 00:20:27.933
of what is now the state of Connecticut.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:32.340
We honor and respect the
enduring relationship

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:36.600
that exists between these peoples
and nations and this land.

00:20:36.600 --> 00:20:38.623
Thank you, and please enjoy the program.

00:20:39.924 --> 00:20:42.924
(people applauding)

00:20:53.670 --> 00:20:57.520
- Mr. President, I have
the honor to present

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:00.240
candidates from Berkeley College

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.630
for the Bachelor's
degrees in Yale college.

00:21:03.630 --> 00:21:06.050
When they have been
recommended by the faculty

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:09.290
of Yale College and
approved by the corporation,

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:12.670
Dean Chun will ask you
by your official act

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:15.838
to confer upon them these degrees.

00:21:15.838 --> 00:21:18.671
(people cheering)

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:24.340
- By the authority vested in me,

00:21:24.340 --> 00:21:27.510
I shall confer upon you
the bachelor's degrees

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:31.480
in Yale College, when
designated by the Dean

00:21:31.480 --> 00:21:33.500
and shall then admit you to all

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:36.333
their rights and responsibilities.

