00:53:40.620 --> 00:53:44.420
- So to the students of the Class of 2021

00:53:44.420 --> 00:53:47.860
and their parents, families and friends

00:53:47.860 --> 00:53:50.733
looking on from around the globe,

00:53:51.950 --> 00:53:55.750
we gather to recognize the
extraordinary accomplishments

00:53:55.750 --> 00:53:58.563
of all of you who have worked so hard

00:53:58.563 --> 00:54:02.113
to complete your programs of study.

00:54:03.550 --> 00:54:07.040
We salute your effort, your diligence,

00:54:07.040 --> 00:54:09.773
your talent, and your intellect.

00:54:11.180 --> 00:54:13.610
We also join you in expressing gratitude

00:54:13.610 --> 00:54:16.790
for all who have supported
you in these endeavors.

00:54:16.790 --> 00:54:19.792
Your families and friends, teachers,

00:54:19.792 --> 00:54:23.183
and other members of the Yale community.

00:54:24.080 --> 00:54:28.312
Congratulations, Class of 2021.

00:54:28.312 --> 00:54:31.145
(people cheering)

00:54:50.170 --> 00:54:52.180
- Hello, Class of 2021.

00:54:52.180 --> 00:54:54.833
I'm Brian Owens, your class secretary.

00:54:55.940 --> 00:54:59.270
Four years have gone by
in the blink of an eye.

00:54:59.270 --> 00:55:02.660
We've made so many memories,
from the first year

00:55:02.660 --> 00:55:05.203
snowball fight on Old Campus right here,

00:55:06.130 --> 00:55:09.040
to the 2019 Yale-Harvard game,

00:55:09.040 --> 00:55:11.163
which we won in double overtime,

00:55:12.120 --> 00:55:15.800
to the late nights, whether
they be in the library

00:55:15.800 --> 00:55:19.630
studying for an exam
or in the common room,

00:55:19.630 --> 00:55:22.253
talking with our suite-mates and friends.

00:55:23.360 --> 00:55:25.370
Although our senior year experience

00:55:25.370 --> 00:55:28.910
has not been a traditional
one, the Class of 2021

00:55:28.910 --> 00:55:30.913
has made the best of the situation.

00:55:32.470 --> 00:55:34.950
When we leave Yale in just a few days,

00:55:34.950 --> 00:55:38.020
we will leave with
memories and friendships

00:55:38.020 --> 00:55:39.363
that last a lifetime.

00:55:40.690 --> 00:55:43.990
Here's to the Class of 2021. We did it.

00:55:43.990 --> 00:55:46.823
(people cheering)

00:56:00.040 --> 00:56:02.310
- Class of 2021, good afternoon.

00:56:02.310 --> 00:56:04.200
My name is Skye Ward, and I am a member

00:56:04.200 --> 00:56:06.838
of the committee that organized Class Day,

00:56:06.838 --> 00:56:11.460
which will air on YouTube
tomorrow at 2:30 PM

00:56:11.460 --> 00:56:14.470
two minutes before two 30 at 2:28 PM,

00:56:14.470 --> 00:56:16.630
a special piece written
by Class Day speaker

00:56:16.630 --> 00:56:19.360
Robert Lopez will be
played from Harkness Tower,

00:56:19.360 --> 00:56:21.240
so keep your ears open.

00:56:21.240 --> 00:56:23.160
If you haven't already
decorated a funny hat

00:56:23.160 --> 00:56:25.030
for Class Day, it's not too late.

00:56:25.030 --> 00:56:26.960
In fact, on your seat today, you received

00:56:26.960 --> 00:56:29.370
a Class Day 2021 hat that
you might want to use

00:56:29.370 --> 00:56:30.730
for that purpose.

00:56:30.730 --> 00:56:33.010
You'll also find a gift
bag, which includes items

00:56:33.010 --> 00:56:35.580
that represent long-standing
Class Day traditions,

00:56:35.580 --> 00:56:36.870
as well as others that are new

00:56:36.870 --> 00:56:39.300
and unique to the class of 2021.

00:56:39.300 --> 00:56:41.130
In addition to the Class Day speaker,

00:56:41.130 --> 00:56:43.040
tomorrow's program also includes remarks

00:56:43.040 --> 00:56:45.140
by members of our class who put together

00:56:45.140 --> 00:56:47.260
outstanding original speeches.

00:56:47.260 --> 00:56:49.670
And because Class Day is about all of us,

00:56:49.670 --> 00:56:52.140
you'll see your own photographs
and video reflections

00:56:52.140 --> 00:56:53.670
throughout tomorrow's program.

00:56:53.670 --> 00:56:57.567
Congratulations, class of
2021, and see you at Class Day.

00:56:57.567 --> 00:57:00.567
(people applauding)

00:57:13.200 --> 00:57:15.610
- Class of 2021, congratulations.

00:57:15.610 --> 00:57:17.470
I am so happy to be with you

00:57:17.470 --> 00:57:19.700
and to celebrate with you today.

00:57:19.700 --> 00:57:21.740
Graduating is a great accomplishment,

00:57:21.740 --> 00:57:24.160
one of the most important
ones of your life.

00:57:24.160 --> 00:57:26.500
If you think back to when
you first arrived on campus,

00:57:26.500 --> 00:57:28.970
though, no one could have
imagined that you would

00:57:28.970 --> 00:57:32.385
live through a global pandemic
before reaching this moment,

00:57:32.385 --> 00:57:36.286
but you did, and thanks to
your strength and perseverance,

00:57:36.286 --> 00:57:39.340
this moment has finally come.

00:57:39.340 --> 00:57:41.010
I'm honored to recognize all the work

00:57:41.010 --> 00:57:42.800
that you have done to get here, much of it

00:57:42.800 --> 00:57:45.420
with the support of
your family and friends.

00:57:45.420 --> 00:57:47.653
today's your day, and it is theirs too.

00:57:48.690 --> 00:57:50.970
Today's a day for looking back with pride

00:57:50.970 --> 00:57:52.790
at everything you have accomplished

00:57:52.790 --> 00:57:55.000
and all the goals you have reached.

00:57:55.000 --> 00:57:57.330
Of course, it brings some sadness too,

00:57:57.330 --> 00:58:00.440
now that you are ending
your bright college years,

00:58:00.440 --> 00:58:02.650
but today's a commencement, a beginning.

00:58:02.650 --> 00:58:06.370
So now as you look to
the days and years ahead,

00:58:06.370 --> 00:58:09.180
think of the new achievements
and opportunities

00:58:09.180 --> 00:58:12.570
in front of you, and look around as well

00:58:12.570 --> 00:58:14.880
to remind yourself of
the excellent company

00:58:14.880 --> 00:58:16.810
joining on this new beginning,

00:58:16.810 --> 00:58:18.523
your friendships formed at Yale.

00:58:20.040 --> 00:58:21.710
Tomorrow you will celebrate Class Day,

00:58:21.710 --> 00:58:24.230
a tradition stretching back 150 years

00:58:24.230 --> 00:58:25.950
in Yale College history.

00:58:25.950 --> 00:58:29.220
I'm excited to watch the
virtual program alongside you,

00:58:29.220 --> 00:58:30.650
and on Monday we can look forward

00:58:30.650 --> 00:58:33.800
to President Salovey's
Commencement address.

00:58:33.800 --> 00:58:35.670
I am grateful to the Class Day committee,

00:58:35.670 --> 00:58:38.450
to the senior class
council, to the University

00:58:38.450 --> 00:58:41.480
Secretary's Office, to your
college heads and deans,

00:58:41.480 --> 00:58:44.170
and to everyone who contributed to making

00:58:44.170 --> 00:58:46.483
the special events of
this weekend possible.

00:58:47.400 --> 00:58:49.770
And I'm most appreciative to you,

00:58:49.770 --> 00:58:52.010
for all that you have brought to Yale

00:58:52.010 --> 00:58:55.080
and will now bring out
to the world with you.

00:58:55.080 --> 00:58:58.286
Again, class of 2021, congratulations

00:58:58.286 --> 00:59:01.286
(people applauding)

00:59:09.148 --> 00:59:11.981
(classical music)

01:06:24.758 --> 01:06:27.341
(upbeat music)

